build: make IPv6 support optional again

Lets an image for a small device leave IPv6 out of the kernel and the packages.
On the TL-WPA7510 v2 that takes 146 KB off the compressed kernel.

Brings back the prompt that 832e7b8172 ("build: always set CONFIG_IPV6") removed
because some packages fail to build without IPv6. Every package of this image
builds without it.

diff --git a/config/Config-build.in b/config/Config-build.in
index 5722c21d41..e8d0c459ab 100644
--- a/config/Config-build.in
+++ b/config/Config-build.in
@@ -204,7 +204,8 @@ menu "Global build settings"
 		  Packages can opt-out via setting PKG_BUILD_FLAGS:=no-mold
 
 	config IPV6
-		def_bool y
+		bool "Enable IPv6 support in packages"
+		default y
 
 	comment "Stripping options"
 
